\ quiet-depth.8th -- Thinking 8th, Chapter 7
\ Verified with: 8th code/ch07/quiet-depth.8th
\
\ Sharing one component (here, whether log actually prints) for two
\ unrelated purposes is fine only if each user restores what it found
\ -- and a depth counter, not a flag, is what makes that safe when the
\ two uses can nest inside each other.

0 var, quiet-depth

: log  \ s --
  quiet-depth @ 0 n:= if . cr else drop then ;

: quiet!    1 quiet-depth n:+! ;
: unquiet!  -1 quiet-depth n:+! ;

"a" log
quiet!
  "b" log
  quiet!
    "c" log
  unquiet!
  "d" log
unquiet!
"e" log

bye
